    <string name="themes_preview_heading">Chapter One. By the Sea</string>
    <string name="themes_preview_text">After dinner I set off along the beach in search of the perfect place to finish my book and start a new one. The sun was sinking toward the horizon, and the long shadows of the trees lay across the sand.</string>
    <string name="themes_preview_text2">“Do you also like reading at sunset?” a stranger asked, without looking up from her page.</string>
    <string name="themes_preview_text3">“Only when the text is easy on the eyes,” I replied. “Font, spacing and margins matter more than you would think.”</string>
    <string name="themes_preview_text4">Extraordinarily characteristic, incomprehensible and uncharacteristically long words are a good test for hyphenation and justified text. Digits 0123456789, “quotes” and punctuation should read easily too.</string>
